{"findings":[{"file":"black.py","line":5766,"what_goes_wrong":"Project-root detection chooses the lexicographically smallest input path instead of their common parent, so an unrelated nested repository can become the root for a multi-source run.","trigger":"Format two directories beneath the current repository where only the first directory contains its own .git directory.","expected":"The common repository root should be selected for both sources.","actual":"The nested .git directory under the first source is selected as the root; later traversal of the other source can raise ValueError because it is outside that root.","confidence":"high","verified_by_running":true,"reproduction":"import tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport black\n\nrepo_root = Path.cwd().resolve()\nwith tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(dir=repo_root) as directory:\n    base = Path(directory)\n    left = base / \"left\"\n    right = base / \"right\"\n    (left / \".git\").mkdir(parents=True)\n    right.mkdir()\n\n    assert black.find_project_root((str(left), str(right))) == repo_root\n"},{"file":"black.py","line":5541,"what_goes_wrong":"Mixed-case valid f-string prefixes such as Fr are not recognized during automatic target-version detection.","trigger":"Format a long function definition containing `Fr\"{value}\"` and a `*args` parameter.","expected":"Because `Fr` is an f-string and therefore requires Python 3.6+, Black should infer that capability and add the safe trailing comma after `*args`.","actual":"Black misses the f-string feature and leaves `*args` without a trailing comma.","confidence":"high","verified_by_running":true,"reproduction":"import black\n\nsource = '''def f(\n    aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa,\n    *args\n):\n    x = Fr\"{value}\"\n'''\nformatted = black.format_str(source, mode=black.Mode())\nassert \"    *args,\\n\" in formatted, formatted\n"}],"what_examined":"I inspected the formatter and daemon control paths, configuration/root discovery, cache and traversal logic, feature autodetection, and relevant tests; I ran Ruff as a lead source, started the project suite, and executed both standalone reproductions above."}
